# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPA fallback for News, scoped deliberately narrowly.
#
# A post published after the last build has no HTML file on the CDN, so Nitro's
# generated "/* /404.html 404" rule would return a 404 before any JavaScript
# runs — and you cannot fetch your way out of a page that never loaded.
#
# This serves the app shell instead for unbuilt News URLs. Vue Router then
# resolves /news/latest/[id] in the browser and useAsyncData fetches the post
# from Sanity, because getCachedData is disabled for News (see data/post.js).
#
# Netlify serves an existing static file in preference to a redirect (there is
# no "!" force flag here), so the ~72 already-built articles keep serving their
# prerendered HTML with full OG tags. Only unbuilt URLs reach this rule.
#
# KNOWN TRADE-OFF: an invalid News URL now returns HTTP 200 with a
# client-rendered error page instead of a real 404 — a "soft 404". Scoped to
# /news/latest/* so the rest of the site keeps returning proper 404s.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/news/latest/*  /200.html  200
